DingoDB multi-license notice
============================

Copyright (c) 2026 Alexander R. Croft

This repository is **not** under a single uniform license. MIT was used only
as temporary scaffolding during project setup. The adopted product license
map is multi-tier (GPL-family track with AGPL for networked bits).

Policy and crate map: `doc/LICENSING.md`

License text files (full terms)
-------------------------------

| File | SPDX | Covers |
|------|------|--------|
| `LICENSE-MIT` | MIT | SDA language, wire format / salvage codec, pure client material |
| `LICENSE-MPL-2.0` | MPL-2.0 | Embedded store, examination host, collection SDK (default features) |
| `LICENSE-AGPL-3.0` | AGPL-3.0-or-later | Cluster, server/serve path, operator CLI |

Per-crate SPDX identifiers are declared in each package’s `Cargo.toml`. Enabling
the optional `cluster` feature on `dingo-sdk` pulls AGPL `dingo-cluster` into
that build (see `doc/LICENSING.md` §4).

How to use this tree
--------------------

- **SDA+ENR1 hybrid** (`dingo-sda`, `dingo-sda-cli`): MIT — see `LICENSE-MIT`.
- **Wire format / thin client** (`dingo-format`, `dingo-client`): MIT — see
  `LICENSE-MIT`.
- **Embedded store / examine / SDK** (`dingo-store`, `dingo-examine`,
  `dingo-sdk` default): MPL-2.0 — see `LICENSE-MPL-2.0`.
- **Networked product** (`dingo-cluster`, `dingo-server`, `dingo-cli`, and
  `dingo-sdk` when built with `features = ["cluster"]`): AGPL-3.0-or-later —
  see `LICENSE-AGPL-3.0`.

Contributions
-------------

By contributing, you license your contribution under the license(s) that apply
to the files you modify (inbound = outbound). See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

This notice is not legal advice. Confirm with counsel for your distribution
model (especially AGPL network use and MPL file-level obligations under
static linking).
